{
  "email": "aisha.khan@brightline.example",
  "reason": "KB-008 quick check: see if payroll verification phishing was caught"
}

{
  "summary": "Reporter: Aisha Khan (HR Generalist, user_id 5) asked whether a circulating \"verify your payroll login\" email is legitimate; she says she heard it is \"going around,\" suggesting multiple recipients. Checked her quarantine: Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain, capital I in place of lowercase l), subject \"Urgent: verify your payroll login,\" received 2026-10-09 08:46 UTC, flagged phishing, not releasable. Her copy was quarantined, so she likely never saw it, and she reports no interaction. Account active, 0 failed logins, not blocked. Escalating per KB-008 (several users likely received it). Needed: security review of the campaign, tenant-wide search/purge for the sender domain and subject, a check for any users who received it and clicked or entered credentials (follow KB-029 for those), and possibly a block on the lookalike domain. Not released, and won't be.",
  "reason": "KB-008: payroll phishing campaign likely hitting several users; security needs to assess scope"
}

{
  "outcome": "escalated",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Aisha, thanks for checking before you did anything. That email is not real. It's a phishing attempt. It came from a fake address made to look like ours ('brightIine-help', with a capital I where the l should be). Our filters caught your copy and it never reached your inbox. Your payroll is not affected, and you don't need to verify anything. If you see this email or one like it: don't click any links, don't reply, and don't forward it to coworkers. Use the Report Phishing button in Outlook, then delete it. If you clicked a link or typed your password anywhere from an email like this, contact us right away so we can secure your account. Since it seems to have gone to other people too, I've passed it to our security team to look into.",
  "internal_note": "Followed KB-008. Found the phishing email in the user's quarantine: Q-1003 from it-support@brightIine-help.example (lookalike domain), subject 'Urgent: verify your payroll login', received 2026-10-09 08:46 UTC, flagged phishing and not releasable. I did not release it. The user reports no interaction, and her copy was quarantined. Account is active with 0 failed logins. She says it is 'going around', which points to several recipients, so I escalated to Tier 2/security (escalation id 1) to check scope, purge it tenant-wide, block the domain and run a KB-029 follow-up for anyone who clicked. Her other quarantined items (Q-1001 open enrollment, Q-1002 gift card spam) were not mentioned and I did not touch them.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-008"
  ],
  "confidence": "high"
}
